name issue_124_bufferbloat_v2
describe 1 Mbps uplink behind a 2 s deep router buffer, every v2 switch on (issue #124)
# `bufferbloat` with the configuration PR #116 makes the default. Measured on main 74266b3, seeds 1-10 (ours / libwebrtc, parity-data of main):
#   cc.queue_p95_ms 57.6-88.6 (mean 69.0) / 47.3 ; video.e2e_delay_p95_ms 92-119 (mean 102.3) / 90.6
#   cc.utilization_pct 91.0-92.3 (mean 91.4) / 92.3 ; cc.target_avg_kbps 934 / 926
# Issue #124 root cause: the test bench sent each 20 ms audio packet at t = 0 mod 20 ms, the phase of the 30 fps video
# frames; libwebrtc's harness sends it at 10 mod 20 (10 ms ADM blocks). Replayed open loop through our GoogCC, libwebrtc's
# packets give libwebrtc's overuse times; ours, with the old phase, gave later ones. With the libwebrtc phase, seeds 1-10:
#   cc.queue_p95_ms 44-55 (mean 49.7) / 47.3 ; video.e2e_delay_p95_ms 75-90 (mean 82.0) / 90.6 ; cc.utilization_pct 90-92 (mean 91.3) / 92.3
# The lines below lock the level reached.
# Target (issue #124): cc.queue_p95_ms within the parity band of libwebrtc (47.3 ms).
duration 40s
at 0s capacity=1000kbps delay=20ms queue=2s
expect cc.queue_p95_ms < 65
expect video.freeze_count == 0
expect audio.mouth_to_ear_p95_ms < 280
expect video.e2e_delay_p95_ms < 100
expect cc.utilization_pct >= 86
